# --- ALE fork additions (surgical; each verified via a controlled getAllFilesFromDir probe) ---
# Our test runs more tools (snpeff/cnvkit/manta/tiddit/hc) and fork-specific features than upstream's
# default test, producing non-deterministic files upstream's patterns don't cover. Excluded from CONTENT
# (stable_path) only — every file still appears as a NAME in stable_name. Deterministic ALE deliverables
# (cn_matrices CSVs, cnvkit .cnr/.cns/.bed, tiddit stats TSVs, README) are KEPT.
# cnvkit plain VCF (##fileDate) + diagram PDF (creation timestamp):
variant_calling/**/*.cnvcall.vcf
variant_calling/**/*.md-diagram.pdf
# fork-only hard-filtered split VCFs + index:
variant_calling_filtered/**/*.vcf.{gz,gz.tbi}
# snpeff QC stats (embed a Date stamp) — our reports/snpeff/<tool>/<sample>/ is one level deeper
# than upstream's reports/snpeff/*/ pattern:
reports/snpeff/**/*_snpEff.csv
reports/snpeff/**/snpEff_summary.html
# mosdepth regions.bed.gz: CONTENT is deterministic (verified by zcat diff), but the bgzf
# BLOCK FRAMING varies with mosdepth's thread scheduling, so the compressed md5 flips
# between runs (caught 2026-08-31; the pre-SVDB snapshot had recorded one byte-variant).
reports/mosdepth/**/*.bed.gz
reports/mosdepth/**/*.bed.gz.csi
# samtools stats (embeds the cram path / command line):
reports/samtools/**/*.stats
# fastp HTML + log: both embed wall-clock values — the HTML footer a timestamp
# ("fastp 0.23.4, at 2026-09-04 10:57:24"), the log a duration ("time used: 1 seconds").
# The log is only INTERMITTENTLY different (it flips when a sample crosses a whole second),
# which makes the test flaky rather than reliably red — caught 2026-09-04. Both became
# relevant when trimming turned on by default. The sibling fastp.json carries the actual
# trimming statistics, is deterministic, and stays snapshotted.
reports/fastp/**/*.{html,log}
# igv-reports dashboard HTML (non-deterministic sessionDictionary) — nested AND top-level
# (** matches subdirs but not direct children of mutation_reports/):
mutation_reports/**/*.html
mutation_reports/*.html
# bundled VCFs + index (gzip framing):
mutation_reports/**/*.vcf.{gz,gz.tbi}
# plain-VCF SVDB merge inputs (data/sv_svdb/merge_inputs/): header ##fileDate is the
# caller's run time, so md5 is run-dependent — assert names only, like the .vcf.gz above
mutation_reports/**/*.vcf
# fork-only TABIX publish dir (bgzipped VCF + index):
tabix/**
# snpeff MultiQC breakdown tables: MultiQC 1.25.1 lists the effect categories of whichever SnpEff
# report it parsed LAST (per-section totals are reset at every file), so the column set follows
# filesystem order — differs between ext4 and the Batch node (output_comparison.md §2.11). Was
# wrongly annotated "SnpEff version-dependent" until 2026-09-09.
multiqc/multiqc_data/*snpeff*.txt
# MultiQC 1.35 (2026-09-24), two new files. multiqc.parquet is the report's data store and differs
# between two runs on identical staged inputs (measured on the e2e MULTIQC task's inputs, run twice).
# llms-full.txt (the report rendered as text) is deterministic on fixed inputs but embeds the
# workflow-summary section, which carries the Nextflow runName — per-execution, like pipeline_info/
# (caught by the e2e pair on 2026-09-24: the only differing line between two runs was runName).
multiqc/multiqc_data/multiqc.parquet
multiqc/multiqc_data/llms-full.txt
# The two early MultiQC reports (2026-09-29: read-QC and alignment-QC, published while the run
# continues). Their data and plots are subsets of the complete report's, whose deterministic files
# stay snapshotted, and they carry the same run-dependent files (llms-full.txt, multiqc.parquet,
# multiqc_data.json, multiqc.log…) — so NAMES only; the e2e asserts their sections explicitly.
multiqc/*-QC_multiqc_report.html
multiqc/*-QC_multiqc_report_data/**
multiqc/*-QC_multiqc_report_plots/**
# The GenBank reference route's snpEff build log (reference/<db>/<db>.snpeff_build.log): snpEff's
# verbose output names the task's work directory and prints elapsed times, so it differs between
# two runs (measured 2026-11-10 on two runs of the test GenBank; the FASTA, GFF3, manifest and the
# four database files next to it were identical and stay snapshotted). NAME only.
reference/*/*.snpeff_build.log
